{
    "background_story": "Jairo was a meticulous and fair-minded professor of mathematics at a prestigious university. His students often joked that he was the toughest grader on campus, but they respected him for it. Jairo believed that grading was not just about assigning numbers, but about providing constructive feedback that would help his students grow. He spent hours poring over each assignment, carefully evaluating every step and providing detailed comments. His students often found themselves challenged to meet his high standards, but they appreciated the effort he put into helping them improve. Jairo's dedication to grading was not just about evaluating performance, but about mentoring and guiding his students towards academic excellence. His reputation as a demanding but fair grader earned him the respect and admiration of his students and colleagues alike.",
